00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:00,100
[WOMAN 1]
It's even on our curtains.

249
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,900
We don't know how he got in.

250
00:11:01,900 --> 00:11:05,567
[WOMAN 2]
We can't figure it out.

251
00:11:05,567 --> 00:11:07,367
Tell the truth, Daboy.

252
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,500
You're friends with
the underwear thief, aren't you?

253
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,567
Huh? Leave me out of this.

254
00:11:11,567 --> 00:11:13,867
Just because there's grease
doesn't mean I'm involved.

255
00:11:13,867 --> 00:11:16,533
- But you're covered in it.
- [DABOY] Come on!

256
00:11:16,533 --> 00:11:17,800
That's sweat!

257
00:11:17,800 --> 00:11:19,400
This is my natural skin color,
okay?

258
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:21,367
- Can I take a look in here?
- [WOMAN 1] Yes. Go ahead.

259
00:11:21,367 --> 00:11:23,367
[BONG] How'd he get in then?

260
00:11:23,367 --> 00:11:27,867
[WOMAN 2] How did that
filthy guy get in here?

261
00:11:27,867 --> 00:11:29,100
Through here.

262
00:11:29,100 --> 00:11:30,633
- [WOMAN 1] What?
- [WOMAN 2 WHIMPERS]

263
00:11:30,633 --> 00:11:31,433
Hold on.

264
00:11:31,433 --> 00:11:32,767
How did he get in?

265
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,233
- Over here.
- This is how he got in?

266
00:11:37,767 --> 00:11:39,833
Right here.
He must've come in this way.

267
00:11:39,833 --> 00:11:41,100
[IPE] Where?

268
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:44,900
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

269
00:11:44,933 --> 00:11:46,767
No one here.

270
00:11:46,767 --> 00:11:48,733
[WOMAN 1] The door
was locked, wasn't it?

271
00:11:48,733 --> 00:11:50,333
[MAN] <i> We got him!
</i> He's over here!

272
00:11:50,333 --> 00:11:51,833
- You heard that?
- [MAN]  Over here!

273
00:11:51,833 --> 00:11:53,400
- They caught him.
- Come on!

274
00:11:54,867 --> 00:11:56,000
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]
- Stay here.

275
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:57,167
They've caught him!

276
00:11:57,167 --> 00:11:59,067
[MEN CLAMORING]

277
00:11:59,067 --> 00:12:00,800
- Come here!
- It's him!

278
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,400
- Come here!
- [GRUNTS]

279
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:05,933
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER,
CLAMORING]

280
00:12:05,933 --> 00:12:07,467
- Get him!
- [BLOW LANDS]

281
00:12:07,467 --> 00:12:09,133
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [SHOUTING]

282
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:10,933
Over here!

283
00:12:10,933 --> 00:12:13,433
- [MEN CLAMORING]
- [PUNCHES LANDING]

284
00:12:13,433 --> 00:12:14,733
What's happening?!

285
00:12:14,767 --> 00:12:16,867
Hey! Stop that!
Come on!

286
00:12:16,867 --> 00:12:18,367
Stop it!

287
00:12:18,367 --> 00:12:20,533
[DABOY] Wait a minute.

288
00:12:20,533 --> 00:12:22,000
They look familiar.

289
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,800
They're not underwear thieves!

290
00:12:23,800 --> 00:12:25,133
They're from Manelco!

291
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,500
Who cares?
Serves them right.

292
00:12:27,500 --> 00:12:28,700
Wait, what do you mean?

293
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,200
They go after people
who use jumpers!

294
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:31,667
That's why our power
keeps getting cut off.

295
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:32,667
Go on, hit 'em some more!

296
00:12:32,667 --> 00:12:34,267
Beat them up
so they'll learn their lesson!

297
00:12:34,267 --> 00:12:36,467
- [CLAMORING]
- Keep going!

298
00:12:36,467 --> 00:12:38,233
Wait! Hold on!

299
00:12:38,233 --> 00:12:39,267
That's enough!

300
00:12:40,567 --> 00:12:43,067
We're the ones at fault here!

301
00:12:43,867 --> 00:12:45,633
We're sorry, sir.

302
00:12:45,633 --> 00:12:47,567
She's right.

303
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,800
You...
You're the ones in the wrong!

304
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:52,033
Haven't I been telling you
for a long time

305
00:12:52,033 --> 00:12:53,133
that it's dangerous

306
00:12:53,133 --> 00:12:55,367
and illegal to tap
into the power lines?

307
00:12:55,367 --> 00:12:57,400
Sir, don't worry.

308
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:59,433
We'll fix this.

309
00:12:59,433 --> 00:13:02,233
We'll find a way to get
a proper power connection.

310
00:13:02,233 --> 00:13:03,233
Okay.

311
00:13:03,233 --> 00:13:04,633
Make sure you do.

312
00:13:04,633 --> 00:13:05,567
Let's go.

313
00:13:05,567 --> 00:13:06,700
Thank you.

314
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:08,433
- Go.
- Get out of here.

315
00:13:08,433 --> 00:13:10,933
- Unbelievable.
- We're done.

316
00:13:10,933 --> 00:13:12,767
- Enough.
- Big mistake.

317
00:13:13,833 --> 00:13:15,400
Gloria.

318
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:18,267
How are we supposed
to get our own electricity?

319
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:22,533
We'll find a way.

320
00:13:22,533 --> 00:13:24,400
We'll figure something out.

321
00:13:24,400 --> 00:13:25,700
All right, all right.

322
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:29,267
I trust you know
what you're doing

323
00:13:29,267 --> 00:13:30,467
We trust you.

324
00:13:30,467 --> 00:13:32,633
Come on, let's get back
to what we were doing.

325
00:13:32,633 --> 00:13:33,867
Let's get to work.

326
00:13:33,867 --> 00:13:36,867
I thought we'd caught
the underwear thief.

327
00:13:36,867 --> 00:13:38,000
Hmph!

328
00:13:40,067 --> 00:13:45,933
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

329
00:13:45,933 --> 00:13:47,733
[DABOY]
Who do you think the thief is?

330
00:13:47,733 --> 00:13:49,567
He's probably from around here.

331
00:13:49,567 --> 00:13:52,267
Someone from outside
wouldn't dare do that here.

332
00:13:52,267 --> 00:13:56,700
At least the thief didn't do
anything else to those women.

333
00:13:56,733 --> 00:13:58,500
But he's still dangerous.

334
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,500
For now,
he's only stealing underwear.

335
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:01,600
But you never know

336
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:04,600
what other sick things
he might think of doing next.

337
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:07,800
Maybe he'll stop now that
that woman has seen him.

338
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,133
He won't stop.

339
00:14:09,133 --> 00:14:10,267
He got away with it.

340
00:14:10,267 --> 00:14:12,533
That'll only encourage him
to do it again.

341
00:14:12,533 --> 00:14:17,867
He'll be even bolder
the next time.

342
00:14:17,867 --> 00:14:19,333
Exactly.

343
00:14:19,333 --> 00:14:21,900
Those women might be the
only victims we know about,

344
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:23,533
but there could be more.

345
00:14:23,533 --> 00:14:25,167
Maybe he started at night,

346
00:14:25,167 --> 00:14:26,667
when no one would notice him.

347
00:14:26,667 --> 00:14:28,800
Then he got bolder and
started doing it during the day.

348
00:14:28,833 --> 00:14:31,467
Then he gets caught and stops,

349
00:14:31,467 --> 00:14:33,933
but the urge comes back,
and he starts doing it again.

350
00:14:33,933 --> 00:14:35,800
Then he won't care
what time it is.

351
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:38,500
[INHALES] That's why
we need to keep an eye out, too.

352
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,867
We have to put an end
to what he's doing.

353
00:14:42,833 --> 00:14:45,533
You're amazing, Gloria.
How did you think of all that?

354
00:14:45,533 --> 00:14:47,300
You're like a detective.

355
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:49,133
A detective? That's right!

356
00:14:49,133 --> 00:14:50,133
[GLORIA SCOFFS]

357
00:14:50,967 --> 00:14:53,600
A detective?
What are you talking about?

358
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:56,767
It's just that my buddies
inside prison

359
00:14:56,767 --> 00:14:58,700
talk about this all the time.

360
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:01,767
They talk about doing
things like that all the time.

361
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,300
- That's all.
- Ah... [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

362
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:07,100
I thought you were good
at investigating.

363
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:08,633
I was going to ask you
to investigate

364
00:15:08,633 --> 00:15:11,100
why the women I'm into
never like me!

365
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:12,200
What are you talking about?

366
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:15,067
All you need is a mirror,
Daboy, not a detective.

367
00:15:15,067 --> 00:15:17,300
You really know
how to ruin the mood.

368
00:15:17,300 --> 00:15:18,733
Don't you have
a mirror at home?

369
00:15:18,733 --> 00:15:20,133
They don't have a home.

370
00:15:21,233 --> 00:15:24,100
Come on. You guys...
Let's go.

371
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,300
Come on.

372
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:29,067
[MAMENG] Trash Talk Junk Shop.

373
00:15:29,067 --> 00:15:30,433
That's quite a mouthful.

374
00:15:30,433 --> 00:15:32,167
- Well...
- Hey!

375
00:15:32,167 --> 00:15:34,733
- Pa!
- We worked hard on that!

376
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:36,267
Oh!

377
00:15:36,267 --> 00:15:40,400
It's done, Gloria, thanks to
Elton and Badong.

378
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:43,900
Wow, it looks beautiful!
Thank you. Thank you so much.

379
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:45,133
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
- [DIDAY] Buddy!

380
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:48,167
This makes us more eager
to collect scrap

381
00:15:48,167 --> 00:15:51,333
now that the junk shop
looks so nice and organized.

382
00:15:51,333 --> 00:15:52,700
And because of that, Gloria,

383
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:55,167
we'll all work harder
to collect more scrap. Right?

384
00:15:55,167 --> 00:15:57,467
- Yeah!
- That's right!

385
00:15:57,467 --> 00:16:03,633
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

386
00:16:03,633 --> 00:16:05,733
What's going on?
A concert? A party?

387
00:16:05,733 --> 00:16:07,400
Hey! Move aside, move aside!

388
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:10,000
What's this? Having fun?

389
00:16:10,033 --> 00:16:12,400
What's going on here?
Why's everyone gathered here?

390
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,833
Cut that out.

391
00:16:13,833 --> 00:16:15,100
Gloria did all this for us.

392
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,333
- Oh, come on.
- What?

393
00:16:16,333 --> 00:16:18,067
You live here,
yet you don't help out.

394
00:16:18,067 --> 00:16:20,767
That's harsh.
Didn't we help?

395
00:16:20,767 --> 00:16:22,533
We showed you earlier.

396
00:16:22,533 --> 00:16:24,867
And you clearly don't need us.

397
00:16:24,867 --> 00:16:27,367
You managed
just fine on your own.

398
00:16:27,367 --> 00:16:29,167
If we'd all worked together,

399
00:16:29,167 --> 00:16:30,700
we could've collected
even more scrap.

400
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:33,433
Yeah, and collected a lot
of resentment, too, right?

401
00:16:33,433 --> 00:16:36,767
You have a lot to say
for someone who didn't help.

402
00:16:36,767 --> 00:16:38,800
This is for our benefit.
You should've cooperated

403
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,700
We didn't want to!
You can't force us.

404
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:42,133
Why are you forcing us?
Are you my mother?

405
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:43,267
- Back off.
- Hey, hey, hey.

406
00:16:43,267 --> 00:16:45,133
Even my own mother
doesn't order me around.

407
00:16:45,133 --> 00:16:46,433
- That's enough.
- Did you hear that?

408
00:16:46,433 --> 00:16:47,767
- You're so full of yourself.
- Hey.

409
00:16:47,767 --> 00:16:49,533
We're just asking
for some cooperation.

410
00:16:49,533 --> 00:16:50,900
- Show a little consideration.
- Oh, really?

411
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:52,400
One, two, three, four, five...

412
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:54,167
- There are so many of you here.
- Shh!

413
00:16:54,167 --> 00:16:56,867
- Okay, that's enough.
- How many more do you need?

414
00:16:56,867 --> 00:16:58,033
- Enough.
- Hmph!

415
00:16:58,033 --> 00:16:58,933
It's already hot out,

416
00:16:58,933 --> 00:17:01,600
so don't let your tempers
flare up, too.

417
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:04,367
Can't we just think about
the good things

418
00:17:04,367 --> 00:17:06,933
that can come from
what we're doing now?

419
00:17:06,933 --> 00:17:08,933
- That's true.
- Sorry, sorry.

420
00:17:08,933 --> 00:17:11,367
Exactly.
They don't appreciate it.

421
00:17:11,367 --> 00:17:13,667
- Come on.
- Gloria's right.

422
00:17:13,667 --> 00:17:16,533
- I'm not so sure!
- You're so lazy!

423
00:17:16,567 --> 00:17:19,000
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

424
00:17:20,433 --> 00:17:27,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

425
00:17:41,933 --> 00:17:48,867
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

426
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:57,300
If it lands on heads...

427
00:17:58,167 --> 00:18:00,433
I'll be able to catch
this syndicate.

428
00:18:06,967 --> 00:18:10,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

429
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:11,100
Heads.

430
00:18:16,567 --> 00:18:23,567
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

431
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:27,867
Taxi!

432
00:18:34,767 --> 00:18:35,933
[DOOR SLAMS]

433
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,467
[ENGINE REVS]

434
00:18:42,133 --> 00:18:49,100
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

435
00:18:56,667 --> 00:19:03,167
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

436
00:19:08,167 --> 00:19:10,333
- [MISTY] Thank you.
- [MAN] You're welcome.

437
00:19:10,333 --> 00:19:12,300
Thank you. Hmm.

438
00:19:14,433 --> 00:19:15,400
[DOOR CLOSES]

439
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:22,367
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

440
00:19:26,933 --> 00:19:28,200
[DOOR CLICKS OPEN]

441
00:19:31,833 --> 00:19:32,933
[DOOR CLOSES]

442
00:19:40,467 --> 00:19:47,467
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

443
00:19:50,367 --> 00:19:51,867
[SAM] We did a lot today.

444
00:19:51,867 --> 00:19:54,533
We should continue with this.
If you see any garbage,

445
00:19:54,533 --> 00:19:56,700
let's segregate and throw them.

446
00:19:56,700 --> 00:20:03,667
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

447
00:20:04,167 --> 00:20:05,333
- Mameng.
- Hmm?

448
00:20:05,833 --> 00:20:08,000
The place looks spacious.
It's beautiful.

449
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,600
I know,
I can't stop looking at it.

450
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,833
- I can't believe it.
- It looks different!

451
00:20:12,833 --> 00:20:15,433
- Is this Ginintuang Lupa?!
- [DANTE] You're right.

452
00:20:15,433 --> 00:20:17,267
- Goodbye, Gloria!
- Bye, Gloria!

453
00:20:17,267 --> 00:20:18,900
- Rest well, guys!
- Good night!

454
00:20:18,900 --> 00:20:20,533
- Goodbye, Gloria!
- Bye!

455
00:20:20,533 --> 00:20:21,500
Bye!

456
00:20:23,433 --> 00:20:25,367
- [DIDAY] Buddy!
- Buddy! [CHUCKLES]

457
00:20:27,300 --> 00:20:29,067
Auntie, Uncle, Pa.

458
00:20:29,667 --> 00:20:30,867
Gloria.

459
00:20:30,867 --> 00:20:34,833
You know, so many politicians
have passed through here

460
00:20:34,833 --> 00:20:38,733
who used us, begging for votes,

461
00:20:38,767 --> 00:20:40,667
then quickly
forgetting about us,

462
00:20:40,667 --> 00:20:43,733
and above all, doing
nothing to change anything.

463
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,767
Pa, sometimes,

464
00:20:46,767 --> 00:20:49,233
we don't have no choice
but to rely on one another.

465
00:20:49,233 --> 00:20:53,167
Who would have thought that
because of one simple woman,

466
00:20:53,167 --> 00:20:56,333
the entire Ginintuang Lupa
would be cleaned.

467
00:20:56,333 --> 00:20:57,100
[DANTE] You're right.

468
00:20:57,200 --> 00:20:59,267
I just did what
I thought was right.

469
00:20:59,267 --> 00:21:00,600
And it wasn't just me!

470
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,567
We all helped each other.

471
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:05,367
I was actually
suprised with them.

472
00:21:05,367 --> 00:21:07,933
I didn't think
they would believe me.

473
00:21:07,933 --> 00:21:11,367
[RUDY] You don't just
go around giving orders.

474
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:13,467
You explain it to them.

475
00:21:13,467 --> 00:21:16,167
And most of all,
you help around too.

476
00:21:17,033 --> 00:21:18,233
[DANTE] To be honest,

477
00:21:18,233 --> 00:21:22,667
bossy people are kind
of exhausting to obey.

478
00:21:22,667 --> 00:21:23,867
That's true.

479
00:21:23,867 --> 00:21:27,967
Gloria has such a good influence
on the people around her.

480
00:21:27,967 --> 00:21:31,833
[MAMENG] Oh, it's not just
with othetr people,

481
00:21:31,833 --> 00:21:34,233
she has such a good
influence on our family too.

482
00:21:34,233 --> 00:21:38,100
And most especially
to her husband, Gabo.

483
00:21:38,100 --> 00:21:42,633
That's what they call G.I.,
good influence.

484
00:21:42,667 --> 00:21:43,800
- Wow.
- See?

485
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:46,033
- You spoke in English.
- Yes, of course!

486
00:21:46,033 --> 00:21:49,133
My nose nearly bled,
but you're right.

487
00:21:49,133 --> 00:21:52,100
- Good job, Mameng.
- Yes, good job.

488
00:21:52,100 --> 00:21:53,267
[LAUGHTER]

489
00:21:53,267 --> 00:21:55,167
Oh no, it's nothing.

490
00:21:55,167 --> 00:21:57,100
I just did what
I thought was right.

491
00:21:57,100 --> 00:21:59,867
And besides,
it doesn't stop here.

492
00:21:59,867 --> 00:22:02,633
We'll continue
doing things right here.

493
00:22:02,633 --> 00:22:03,933
[DANTE] Thank you, Gloria.

494
00:22:03,933 --> 00:22:07,200
- Yay.
- [APPLAUDING]

495
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:09,633
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

496
00:22:09,633 --> 00:22:16,567
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

497
00:22:22,033 --> 00:22:23,500
[MAN] Let's do one game.

498
00:22:27,533 --> 00:22:28,967
Come on! It's our treat.

499
00:22:29,367 --> 00:22:30,333
[WOMAN] Pass.

500
00:22:30,333 --> 00:22:31,767
[MAN] We're at a billiards hall.

501
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:33,167
Can't we get to know people?

502
00:22:33,167 --> 00:22:35,600
It's just a friendly game.
It's not a proposal.

503
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,300
[WOMAN] I said
we're not interested.

504
00:22:38,267 --> 00:22:39,700
[MAN] Wow, turning me
down right away?

505
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:44,400
You're so pretty,
but so grumpy.

506
00:22:44,733 --> 00:22:47,433
[WOMAN] Rejecting someone
doesn't mean we're being grumpy.

507
00:22:49,767 --> 00:22:51,400
[BILLIARD BALLS CLACKING]

508
00:22:55,133 --> 00:22:56,600
[MAN] Come on!
Just one rack.

509
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:58,700
You're so grumpy.

510
00:23:03,100 --> 00:23:04,567
[GABO] Uh, miss.

511
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:08,767
Uh, is it okay if
I join you?

512
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,367
Guys.

513
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:16,267
- Hey, miss!
- Stop being so persistent.

514
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,700
Well, if you haven't heard...

515
00:23:20,767 --> 00:23:23,167
I'm Efren "Bata" Reyes'
grandson.

516
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:24,133
How about this?

517
00:23:25,033 --> 00:23:26,600
Play against me instead.

518
00:23:27,233 --> 00:23:28,267
In what?

519
00:23:28,267 --> 00:23:29,267
- In billiards!
- Watch

520
00:23:29,267 --> 00:23:31,033
- how I sink this, okay?
- Billiards. [SCOFFS]

521
00:23:34,433 --> 00:23:35,367
[MISTY] Here's my deal.

522
00:23:35,733 --> 00:23:37,200
If you win,

523
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:40,067
I'll pay for all your drinks

524
00:23:40,067 --> 00:23:42,400
and your games
for the whole day.

525
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:44,533
I'll even be your spotter.

526
00:23:44,533 --> 00:23:47,300
But if you lose,

527
00:23:47,300 --> 00:23:49,533
you guys will leave them alone.

528
00:23:49,933 --> 00:23:50,900
Go.

529
00:23:50,900 --> 00:23:51,867
- Deal?
- Deal!

530
00:23:51,867 --> 00:23:53,033
- Deal!
- Deal.

531
00:23:53,033 --> 00:23:54,033
Deal.

532
00:23:54,633 --> 00:23:56,900
Let's do this. Come on!

533
00:23:56,933 --> 00:23:58,367
- Whoo!
- That's nothing.

534
00:24:02,667 --> 00:24:05,567
[BILLIARD BALLS CLACKING]

535
00:24:08,033 --> 00:24:09,533
[BILLIARD BALLS CLACKING]

536
00:24:10,833 --> 00:24:14,433
- [BILLIARD BALLS CLACKING]
- [CLAPPING]

537
00:24:15,467 --> 00:24:22,400
- [BILLIARD BALLS CLACKING]
- [UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

538
00:24:35,900 --> 00:24:42,833
- [BILLIARD BALLS CLACKING]
- [UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

539
00:24:53,767 --> 00:24:55,967
[BILLIARD BALLS CLACKING]

540
00:24:57,733 --> 00:24:58,800
What now?

541
00:25:00,033 --> 00:25:01,800
You can go now. Go!

542
00:25:04,333 --> 00:25:06,167
Miss! Thank you again.

543
00:25:06,167 --> 00:25:07,633
Those guys were so persistent.

544
00:25:07,967 --> 00:25:11,267
You're welcome. But you know,
I can't blame those boys

545
00:25:11,267 --> 00:25:13,600
because you're all so pretty.

546
00:25:14,300 --> 00:25:16,900
Actually, you're exactly
the type I'm looking for.

547
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:18,867
- Us?
- Yes.

548
00:25:19,067 --> 00:25:20,867
I work for a modeling agency,

549
00:25:20,867 --> 00:25:23,900
and tomorrow we have
a pictorial.

550
00:25:24,100 --> 00:25:25,533
Would you like to come?

551
00:25:25,833 --> 00:25:28,233
Tomorrow? Sure! How?

552
00:25:28,567 --> 00:25:29,467
Wait.

553
00:25:31,833 --> 00:25:33,700
Save your numbers here.

554
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:35,133
I'll give you my number.

555
00:25:36,833 --> 00:25:39,233
I will text you
all the details, okay?

556
00:25:39,233 --> 00:25:40,833
But I'll see you tomorrow.

557
00:25:40,833 --> 00:25:41,933
- Okay.
- You're in?

558
00:25:41,933 --> 00:25:42,900
We're in!

559
00:25:42,900 --> 00:25:44,167
See you, girls.

560
00:25:44,167 --> 00:25:45,633
Take care!

561
00:25:46,800 --> 00:25:49,033
- Bye! Stay pretty!
- Bye!

562
00:25:51,567 --> 00:25:53,533
[BILLIARD BALLS CLACKING]

563
00:25:56,800 --> 00:25:58,100
Uh, ladies.

564
00:25:58,533 --> 00:25:59,967
Uh, thank you, alright?

565
00:26:00,467 --> 00:26:02,267
See you around sometime?

566
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:03,733
Thank you.

567
00:26:09,767 --> 00:26:15,033
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

568
00:26:15,033 --> 00:26:16,167
[GABO] Move the car.

569
00:26:16,167 --> 00:26:17,433
Pick up the woman in white.

570
00:26:23,700 --> 00:26:24,767
[DIGITAL TRILLING]

571
00:26:26,133 --> 00:26:27,200
Wait.

572
00:26:27,800 --> 00:26:29,000
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

573
00:26:30,433 --> 00:26:31,367
[MISTY] Uh...

574
00:26:35,033 --> 00:26:36,467
To Ridgetown, QC, please.

575
00:26:36,467 --> 00:26:37,467
[GABO GRUNTS]

576
00:26:37,467 --> 00:26:39,767
Sorry, ma'am.
I just used the restroom.

577
00:26:39,767 --> 00:26:41,267
What the...

578
00:26:41,267 --> 00:26:43,200
How did the taxi move earlier?

579
00:26:43,233 --> 00:26:44,867
- Oh. Uh...
- [ENGINE REVVING]

580
00:26:45,467 --> 00:26:48,667
My car's pretty high-tech,
ma'am.

581
00:26:48,667 --> 00:26:49,733
Where are you headed?

582
00:26:50,733 --> 00:26:53,200
Ridgetown, QC.

583
00:26:53,700 --> 00:26:55,767
Ridgetown, QC.
Coming right up!

584
00:26:58,033 --> 00:27:01,267
You know, this is my first time
riding a car

585
00:27:01,267 --> 00:27:04,067
that moves without a driver.

586
00:27:04,433 --> 00:27:08,233
It's the only car of this kind
here in the Philippines.

587
00:27:08,233 --> 00:27:10,167
It's actually imported.

588
00:27:10,167 --> 00:27:14,300
Straight from Japan with love,
love, love, love. [CHUCKLES]

589
00:27:14,300 --> 00:27:15,400
You know...

590
00:27:16,200 --> 00:27:19,133
You'd be perfect if you
just stopped calling me "ma'am".

591
00:27:19,133 --> 00:27:20,300
I'm sorry, ma'am.

592
00:27:20,300 --> 00:27:22,233
There you go again.

593
00:27:22,233 --> 00:27:23,433
[GABO] I'm really sorry, ma'am.

594
00:27:23,433 --> 00:27:25,767
I'm just used to saying it.

595
00:27:25,767 --> 00:27:27,333
[MISTY] How about...

596
00:27:27,333 --> 00:27:29,633
you stop being so respectful?

597
00:27:30,467 --> 00:27:32,467
W-What do you mean, ma'am?

598
00:27:33,100 --> 00:27:34,133
You want me to disrespect you?

599
00:27:35,833 --> 00:27:37,067
You know...

600
00:27:37,567 --> 00:27:39,167
It's a good thing you're cute.

601
00:27:39,167 --> 00:27:41,567
Otherwise, you'd be getting
on my nerves.

602
00:27:42,033 --> 00:27:44,733
Pull over to the side for a bit.

603
00:27:44,733 --> 00:27:46,733
- Why, ma'am?
- Pull over.

604
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:49,200
[GABO] Are you angry?

605
00:27:49,233 --> 00:27:52,233
Did I annoy you
with what I said?

606
00:27:53,500 --> 00:27:55,633
No. I just want to move up front

607
00:27:55,633 --> 00:27:58,133
because I'm getting dizzy
back here.

608
00:27:58,133 --> 00:27:59,767
And...

609
00:27:59,833 --> 00:28:04,633
I want to see up close
if you're really that cute.

610
00:28:04,633 --> 00:28:06,000
[MISTY] Come on. Pull over.

611
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:10,867
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

612
00:28:10,867 --> 00:28:11,867
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

613
00:28:19,100 --> 00:28:20,433
- Better now, ma'am?
- Phew.

614
00:28:20,433 --> 00:28:21,900
Much better.

615
00:28:21,900 --> 00:28:23,433
[SENSUAL MUSIC PLAYING]

616
00:28:23,467 --> 00:28:25,800
[MISTY]
The view's better from here.

617
00:28:25,800 --> 00:28:26,900
[GABO CHUCKLES]

618
00:28:26,900 --> 00:28:28,333
So, ma'am...

619
00:28:28,933 --> 00:28:31,233
Am I cuter up close?

620
00:28:31,733 --> 00:28:32,967
Confirmed!

621
00:28:32,967 --> 00:28:35,000
You're cuter up close.

622
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:38,867
But I don't even know your name.

623
00:28:38,867 --> 00:28:41,033
Uh, ma'am...

624
00:28:41,900 --> 00:28:44,133
I'm Gabriel Magtibay.

625
00:28:44,133 --> 00:28:46,200
But you can just call me Gabo.

626
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:47,233
Gabo?

627
00:28:47,800 --> 00:28:49,333
I'm Misty.

628
00:28:51,233 --> 00:28:52,467
Gabo.

629
00:28:52,467 --> 00:28:54,067
Nice to meet you, Gabo.

630
00:28:54,067 --> 00:28:55,967
[CHUCKLES]
Nice to meet you too.

631
00:28:57,200 --> 00:28:59,967
Are you a nurse, ma'am?

632
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:02,167
Me? Uh...

633
00:29:02,167 --> 00:29:06,467
No, but I'm taking
some nursing classes.

634
00:29:06,967 --> 00:29:10,700
Oh, that explains why
you're so beautiful.

635
00:29:10,700 --> 00:29:12,433
[SENSUAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

636
00:29:12,433 --> 00:29:13,733
What about you, Gabo?

637
00:29:14,567 --> 00:29:15,933
Where are you from?

638
00:29:15,933 --> 00:29:20,000
From Ginintuang Lupa, Tondo,
ma'am.

639
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:21,600
You can ask anyone there.

640
00:29:21,600 --> 00:29:22,767
Everyone knows me.

641
00:29:23,267 --> 00:29:24,867
- Is that so?
- [GABO CHUCKLES]

642
00:29:25,633 --> 00:29:28,633
How about you, ma'am?
Where in Manila are you from?

643
00:29:28,633 --> 00:29:31,033
I'm actually from the province,

644
00:29:31,067 --> 00:29:34,400
so I don't know
my way around here.

645
00:29:34,400 --> 00:29:36,600
Have you been in Manila long?

646
00:29:39,233 --> 00:29:40,633
Yes, but...

647
00:29:42,233 --> 00:29:43,767
I don't go out much.

648
00:29:43,767 --> 00:29:45,900
That's why I'm not familiar
with the roads.

649
00:29:45,900 --> 00:29:47,867
Well, if you'd like, ma'am,

650
00:29:47,867 --> 00:29:49,600
you could hire me full-time.

651
00:29:49,600 --> 00:29:51,333
I'll be your personal driver.

652
00:29:51,333 --> 00:29:53,633
I'll drive you anywhere,
day or night.

653
00:29:53,633 --> 00:29:55,133
Wherever you need to go,

654
00:29:55,133 --> 00:29:57,567
I'll make sure
you get there on time

655
00:29:57,567 --> 00:29:59,933
and never get lost.

656
00:29:59,933 --> 00:30:02,633
And with me driving,
you'll be safe, too.

657
00:30:02,667 --> 00:30:04,333
[SENSUAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

658
00:30:04,333 --> 00:30:05,467
Sounds good.

659
00:30:06,333 --> 00:30:08,067
What do you mean?

660
00:30:08,067 --> 00:30:09,500
I think it's a good idea.

661
00:30:09,500 --> 00:30:13,900
So you'll be my regular driver
from now on?

662
00:30:13,900 --> 00:30:16,367
Really, ma'am? Alright!

663
00:30:16,367 --> 00:30:17,733
[CHUCKLES]

664
00:30:17,733 --> 00:30:19,067
Don't worry, ma'am.

665
00:30:19,067 --> 00:30:20,867
I'll keep you safe.

666
00:30:20,867 --> 00:30:23,733
You'll never get lost,
and you'll always arrive on time

667
00:30:23,733 --> 00:30:25,867
for your meetings.

668
00:30:25,867 --> 00:30:26,967
Leave it to me.

669
00:30:26,967 --> 00:30:29,900
- Alright. Game.
- [GABO] Game!

670
00:30:29,900 --> 00:30:31,867
- Let's do this!
- Let's do this!

671
00:30:31,867 --> 00:30:33,133
[GABO LAUGHS]

672
00:30:33,133 --> 00:30:34,400
[SENSUAL MUSIC FADES]

673
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:38,467
<i>How did the NCIA
track down our businesses?</i>

674
00:30:38,500 --> 00:30:41,667
<i>I've never felt this way
about a man before.</i>

675
00:30:41,667 --> 00:30:43,567
<i> You're so lucky, Gabo.</i>

676
00:30:43,567 --> 00:30:45,767
<i>Why don't you
just move in here?</i>

677
00:30:45,767 --> 00:30:47,000
<i> Let's live together.</i>

678
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:50,000
<i>Looks like Gabo
will be home late.</i>

679
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:52,233
<i> Maybe he found a job.</i>

680
00:30:52,233 --> 00:30:53,400
<i>- Ma'am.
- Misty!</i>

681
00:30:53,800 --> 00:30:54,667
<i> Boss?</i>
